          "jcr:created": "Thu Feb 06 2025 18:52:38 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Overview</span></h2>\n<p>The Skeletal Anchoring&nbsp;System is a bone borne temporary anchorage device comprised of titanium anchor screws and plates. This system is designed for use as an anchor in orthodontic procedures such as intrusion/extrusion of teeth, space closure, distal/mesial movement, and 3D control of teeth.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Apr 02 2025 21:27:04 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
